   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3. Hypotheses\n",
    "\n",
    "For each KPI:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **H0** — the Test and Control distributions are the same\n",
    "- **H1** — they differ\n",
    "\n",
    "Both tests are two-sided -> a redesign can just as easily make things worse, and we want to be able to see that if it happens!!\n",
    "\n",
    "#### We only test the completion rate, not the noncompletion rate. The two always add up to 100%, so they're the same fact stated twice:\n",
    "-> Control is 65.59% / 34.41% ; Test is 69.29% / 30.71%. \n",
    "\n",
    "-> Testing both would give the same p-value twice and make the multiple-comparison correction more difficult for no reason.\n",
    "\n",
    "-> Noncompletion is reported as a descriptive figure only."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a2f79cd3-918a-4147-9fde-6d2b5f95958e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### RQ1 Statistical Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The Control group had a completion rate of 65.59%, while the Test group had a completion rate of 69.29%.\n",
    "\n",
    "The Test group therefore achieved an absolute improvement of 3.71 percentage points and a relative improvement of 5.65%.\n",
    "\n",
    "A one tailed two proportion Z test produced a Z statistic of 8.8745. At an alpha level of 0.05, the critical value was 1.6449.\n",
    "\n",
    "Because the test statistic exceeded the critical value and the p value was below 0.05, the null hypothesis was rejected.\n",
    "\n",
    "The 95% confidence interval for the difference in completion rates ranged from 2.89 to 4.53 percentage points. Since the entire interval is above zero, the result supports a positive improvement in the Test group.\n",
    "\n",
    "Cohen's h was 0.0791, indicating a small effect size.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Decision\n",
    "\n",
    "Reject H0.\n",
    "\n",
    "There is statistically significant evidence that the redesigned digital process increased the client completion rate compared with the existing process.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The redesign improved completion by approximately 3.71 percentage points. Although the statistical effect size is small, the improvement is consistent and statistically reliable across the large client sample.\n",
    "\n",
    "The redesigned process should therefore be considered beneficial for completion performance, while other usability measures should also be reviewed before making a final implementation recommendation."
   ]
