    "    label=f\"LCV = {critical_value:.4f}\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test statistic\n",
    "plt.axvline(\n",
    "    z_stat,\n",
    "    linestyle=\":\",\n",
    "    label=f\"Test Statistic = {z_stat:.4f}\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.title(\"RQ3: Mann-Whitney U Test Critical Value\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Z Statistic\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Probability Density\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b2c7b450-fcec-4902-85fd-bc0de38e7d11",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### RQ3 Statistical Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The Control group had a median completion time of 4.52 minutes, while the Test group had a median completion time of 3.95 minutes.\n",
    "\n",
    "The redesigned process reduced the median completion time by approximately 0.57 minutes, equivalent to about 34 seconds or a 12.55% reduction.\n",
    "\n",
    "Completion times were strongly positively skewed in both groups. Control skewness was 8.69 and Test skewness was 7.38. Using the IQR method, 2,705 observations were identified as outliers, representing 8.25% of completed clients. These observations were retained because they may represent genuine client behavior during the process.\n",
    "\n",
    "Because the completion time distributions were highly skewed and contained substantial outliers, a one tailed Mann Whitney U test was used.\n",
    "\n",
    "The Mann Whitney U statistic was 120,771,157.50 with a p value below 0.05.\n",
    "\n",
    "Using the large sample normal approximation, the test statistic was Z = negative 14.6719. At an alpha level of 0.05, the lower critical value was negative 1.6449.\n",
    "\n",
    "Since the test statistic was below the lower critical value and the p value was below 0.05, the null hypothesis was rejected.\n",
    "\n",
    "The rank biserial correlation was 0.0939, indicating a very small effect size.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Decision\n",
    "\n",
    "Reject H0.\n",
    "\n",
    "There is statistically significant evidence that clients using the redesigned Test process complete the process faster than clients using the Control process.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The redesigned process reduced the typical completion time from 4.52 minutes to 3.95 minutes.\n",
    "\n",
    "This represents a median saving of approximately 34 seconds per completed client and a 12.55% reduction in completion time.\n",
    "\n",
    "Although the statistical effect size is very small, the reduction in median completion time is operationally relevant because even modest time savings can accumulate across a large number of digital client interactions.\n",
    "\n",
    "This result provides evidence that the redesigned process improved processing efficiency. However, it should be considered together with completion rate, Step Back behavior, navigation errors, and funnel bottlenecks before making the final deployment recommendation."
   ]
  },
