   "id": "2f5fedc9-cd91-4685-8888-9c4a50215d9f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### RQ4 Statistical Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The Control group recorded an average of 0.407 Step Back events\n",
    "per client, while the Test group recorded an average of 0.602.\n",
    "\n",
    "Both groups had a median of 0 Step Back events because most\n",
    "clients did not navigate backward during the process.\n",
    "\n",
    "The Step Back count distributions were strongly positively skewed.\n",
    "Control skewness was 3.31 and Test skewness was 4.10.\n",
    "\n",
    "Because Step Back count was highly skewed and contained many zero\n",
    "values, a one tailed Mann Whitney U test was used.\n",
    "\n",
    "The Mann Whitney U statistic was 342,403,506 with a one sided\n",
    "p value of 1.000.\n",
    "\n",
    "At an alpha level of 0.05, the lower critical value for the\n",
    "left tailed normal approximation was -1.6449. The standardized\n",
    "test statistic was Z = 15.3577, which was outside the rejection\n",
    "region.\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, the null hypothesis was not rejected.\n",
    "\n",
    "The rank biserial correlation was 0.0791, indicating a very small\n",
    "effect size.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Decision\n",
    "\n",
    "Fail to reject H0.\n",
    "\n",
    "There is insufficient evidence that clients using the redesigned\n",
    "Test process experienced fewer Step Back events than clients using\n",
    "the Control process.\n",
    "\n",
    "In fact, the descriptive results show that the Test group had a\n",
    "higher average Step Back count of 0.602 compared with 0.407 in\n",
    "the Control group.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The redesigned process did not reduce backward navigation behavior.\n",
    "\n",
    "Clients in the Test group used Step Back more frequently on\n",
    "average than clients in the Control group. However, the very small\n",
    "rank biserial effect size indicates that the overall distributional\n",
    "difference between the groups was limited.\n",
    "\n",
    "This suggests that the redesigned process may still contain areas\n",
    "of navigation friction.\n",
    "\n",
    "This finding should be examined together with stage level funnel\n",
    "performance to determine where clients are most likely to encounter\n",
    "difficulty."
   ]
  },
