   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d7ae6177-c83a-4289-8eb4-907c38d56135",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### RQ5 Statistical Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "The two proportion Z tests show that the effect of the new digital experience differs across the customer journey.\n",
    "\n",
    "For **start → step_1**, the Test group achieved a conversion rate of **90.71%**, compared with **85.83%** for Control. The difference of **4.88 percentage points** was statistically significant, with **Z = -17.035** and **p < 0.001**. Therefore, the null hypothesis was rejected. This provides strong evidence that the Test experience improved initial customer progression.\n",
    "\n",
    "For **step_1 → step_2**, the Test conversion rate was **91.66%**, compared with **92.46%** for Control. The Test group performed **0.80 percentage points lower**, and the difference was statistically significant, with **Z = 3.109** and **p = 0.0019**. Therefore, the null hypothesis was rejected. This indicates a statistically significant deterioration at this stage of the Test experience.\n",
    "\n",
    "For **step_2 → step_3**, the Test conversion rate was **93.60%**, compared with **93.06%** for Control. The Test group improved by approximately **0.54 percentage points**. The difference was statistically significant, with **Z = -2.187** and **p = 0.0288**. Therefore, the null hypothesis was rejected, although the practical improvement was relatively small.\n",
    "\n",
    "For **step_3 → confirm**, the Test conversion rate was **88.33%**, compared with **87.99%** for Control. Although Test was approximately **0.35 percentage points higher**, the difference was not statistically significant, with **Z = -1.049** and **p = 0.2943**. Therefore, we fail to reject the null hypothesis.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Decision\n",
    "\n",
    "The Test experience did not improve every stage of the customer journey equally. Its strongest and most meaningful improvement occurred at **start → step_1**, while **step_1 → step_2 showed a statistically significant decline**. The improvement at **step_2 → step_3 was statistically significant but small**, and there was insufficient evidence of a difference at **step_3 → confirm**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Business Implication\n",
    "\n",
    "Vanguard should retain the elements of the Test experience that improve initial engagement, while investigating the **step_1 → step_2 transition** for possible friction. The final confirmation stage should not be claimed as an improvement because the observed difference was not statistically significant."
   ]
  },
